From 593908cf1ca3b522dd9adef7ebd70793ea3ad148 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gabe Ochoa <urgentcactus@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 08:16:47 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] e2e: barriers, isolated storage, visible-rect targets,
 Unicode type, test clipboard, native_resize, logical coordinates

Native/headless test support that apps were each working around:

- await_frame [timeout]: blocks the script until two UI render passes
  after it (layout and render both reflect state), failing at a wall-clock
  deadline. PendingE2ECommand::block_until() makes any command a runner
  barrier with a wall-clock deadline instead of the 30-tick budget.
- AFTERHOURS_TEST_STORAGE_DIR / files::isolate_storage(): config, saves and
  the new temp path move together under one test root; platform folders are
  neither read nor created.
- get_visible_rect/is_visible: screen rect cut by every scroll/clip ancestor
  and the window (the renderer's clip). Named/text clicks use the visible
  part and fail when fully clipped; assert_ui visible=, vx/vy/vw/vh; dump_ui
  marks clipped nodes.
- type decodes UTF-8 to code points (push_char(int), push_text).
- register_builtin_handlers installs an in-memory clipboard;
  set_clipboard / expect_clipboard; use_system_clipboard() opts out.
- native_resize w h [timeout]: resizes the real window, waits for the
  backend size plus a render; "unsupported" headless.
- Script coordinates and rect reports are logical pixels (screen / ui_scale
  in Adaptive mode).

Tests: e2e_barrier_test, files_isolated_storage_test, e2e_visibility_test,
e2e_zoom_coordinates_test (1.0/1.4/2.0), e2e_unicode_type_test,
e2e_clipboard_test, native_resize_test (+ make native-window-test).
