@@ -30,6 +30,7 @@ Started partway through the project's life, so it does not go all the way back.
 - **Menu shortcuts sit one pad in from the panel edge** — they were flush, clipping the last glyph in half.
 
 ### New APIs
+- **Isolated storage for test runs.** Set `AFTERHOURS_TEST_STORAGE_DIR` (`files::TEST_STORAGE_ENV`) and `ProvidesResourcePaths` puts config, saves and the new temp path under `<dir>/{config,save,tmp}/<game>`, without reading or creating the platform folders. `files::isolate_storage(dir)` does the same for an already-initialised provider. `files::get_temp_path()` / `temp_folder_path` are new; temp defaults to the OS temp dir.
 - **`polyline::draw_dashed(pts, thickness, color, dash, gap, phase)`** (`polyline.h`) draws a patterned run. `draw_line_ex` was solid-only, so a dashed cable, marquee or tick run had to be hand-rolled. Arc length accumulates across vertices, so a dash straddling a corner stays one dash, and `phase` is what animates it.
 - **`polyline::resample_by_arclength(pts, step)`** returns evenly spaced points. A bezier sampler walks uniformly in `t`, which is not uniform in screen distance, so anything spaced along the result bunches where the curve is tight.
 - **`draw_line_ex` is recorded by capture**, so a test can assert on a dashed pattern. The `none` backend used to log `@notimplemented` and draw nothing.
@@ -80,6 +81,13 @@ Started partway through the project's life, so it does not go all the way back.
 - **`SINGLETON_FWD` still does not work in class scope** — use `SINGLETON_CLASS_FWD`, which has existed since `e9c662b`. Comment-only change.
 
 ### e2e
+- **E2E coordinates are logical pixels.** `click`/`mouse_move`/`drag`/... arguments, `double_click_ui` offsets, `assert_ui x/y/w/h`, `dump_ui`, `expect_drawn_at`/`dump_draws` and `assert_no_overflow` reports used screen pixels, so every number in a script went stale when an Adaptive-mode app zoomed. They are now divided by `ui_scale` (Adaptive only; Proportional ignores `ui_scale`, so nothing changes there, and nothing changes anywhere at 100%). `N%` stays a fraction of the window. `ui_commands::get_screen_rect` and the injector still use screen pixels. *What to do:* a script that hard-codes screen pixels at a zoom other than 100% needs those numbers divided by the zoom.
+- **E2E scripts get their own clipboard.** `register_builtin_handlers` installs an in-memory provider (`testing::test_clipboard()`), so test copy/paste never reads or overwrites the user's clipboard and works with no window. `set_clipboard "text"` and `expect_clipboard "text"` seed and check it; it empties on `reset_test_state` and between scripts. *What to do:* to test the platform clipboard on purpose, call `testing::use_system_clipboard()` after registering.
+- **`await_frame [timeout_s]`** holds the script until a frame whose layout and render both ran after it (two UI render passes, counted by `VisibleTextRegistry::generation`), and fails with the render count at the deadline (default 5s). A host that batches several ticks per render could click a view that was never drawn.
+- **`PendingE2ECommand::block_until(seconds)`** makes any command a barrier: the runner dispatches nothing after it until it resolves, and it is timed by a wall-clock deadline instead of the 30-tick budget. `retry()` alone still lets later lines run.
+- **Clicks aim at what is visible.** `ui_commands::get_visible_rect` / `is_visible` cut the screen rect by every scroll/clip ancestor and the window, using the renderer's own clip. `click_ui`, `click_text`, `click_button`, the right-click variants, `toggle_checkbox`, `select_dropdown`, `set_slider` and `double/triple_click_ui` click the visible part and fail naming the target when it is fully clipped. `assert_ui` gains `visible=true|false` and `vx/vy/vw/vh`; `dump_ui` adds `visible="partial|false"` and the visible rect on clipped nodes only.
+- **`type` accepts UTF-8.** The injected char queue carries Unicode code points (`test_input::push_char(int)`, new `push_text(utf8)`), so `type "héllo 日本 🎉"` reaches text fields intact instead of as negative bytes. Malformed bytes become U+FFFD.
+- **`native_resize w h [timeout_s]`** resizes the real window and holds the script until the backend reports that size in logical points and a UI render has followed. Headless and backend-less builds fail with "unsupported" (use `resize`). On sokol/Metal it goes through the app's `metal_set_window_size`.
 - **The harness ships with the engine** (`e2e_testing/harness.h`): `E2EArgs`, `parse_e2e_args`, `should_run_e2e`, `screenshot_path`, `count_e2e_scripts`, `configure_runner`. Every consumer was writing its own ~150 line parser and they had drifted. New flags while there: `--screenshot-dir` and `--e2e-speed` (an accepted spelling of `--time-scale`).
 - **`wait_frames N` waits N frames.** It stored `N/60` seconds and the runner counted that down with `dt`, so it was a frame count only if the host ticked at exactly 60Hz, and `--time-scale` changed it again. Whether a suite was reproducible was the host's undocumented decision.
 - **`right_click_ui <name>` and `right_click_text "..."`** open a context menu the way the app does. A secondary click could only be aimed at a coordinate, which goes stale the moment the layout moves.
diff --git a/docs/plugins.md b/docs/plugins.md
index e417cc0..8085e9e 100644
--- a/docs/plugins.md
+++ b/docs/plugins.md
@@ -125,6 +125,34 @@ Quote arguments containing spaces: `assert_ui header "text=My Project" hidden=fa
 
 Text commands such as `type`, `expect_text` and the value in `expect_input_text` still accept the unquoted rest of the line verbatim. To use escapes there, quote the entire text. Custom handlers receive decoded arguments and should not tokenize them again.
 
+## E2E barriers and deadlines
+
+`await_frame [timeout_s]` blocks the script until two UI render passes have happened after it, so the next command sees a layout and a render that both ran after every earlier line. It fails at the deadline (default 5 seconds) with the number of renders seen. A host that never runs the UI render pass with `AFTER_HOURS_ENABLE_E2E_TESTING` always times out.
+
+A custom handler that waits on a worker, an asset or the network calls `cmd.block_until(seconds)` on every visit until it can consume or fail. That holds the runner and replaces the 30-tick timeout with a wall-clock deadline. `cmd.retry()` alone keeps the command pending but lets later lines run.
+
+## E2E coordinates
+
+Script coordinates and reported rectangles are logical pixels: screen pixels divided by `ui_scale` in Adaptive mode, screen pixels in Proportional mode. `N%` is a fraction of the window. Logical units apply to coordinate commands, `double_click_ui` offsets, `assert_ui` and `dump_ui`, `expect_drawn_at` and `dump_draws`, and `assert_no_overflow`. A widget built at `pixels(100)` asserts as `w=100` at 100%, 140% and 200%. C++ helpers such as `get_screen_rect` stay in screen pixels; use `testing::e2e_to_logical` and `testing::e2e_ui_scale` to convert.
+
+## E2E visibility
+
+`ui_commands::get_visible_rect(entity)` is the screen rectangle cut by every scroll or clip ancestor and by the window, using the same clip as rendering and hit testing. `is_visible` requires at least one whole pixel. Named and text clicks target the centre of the visible part, skip fully clipped matches and fail with "fully clipped" when nothing visible matches. `assert_ui name visible=false` and `vx`/`vy`/`vw`/`vh` assert it; `dump_ui` adds `visible` and `v*` attributes only to clipped nodes.
+
+## E2E text and clipboard
+
+`type` decodes UTF-8 and queues one Unicode code point per character, as the native backends deliver them. Invalid bytes become U+FFFD.
+
+`register_builtin_handlers` installs an in-memory clipboard for the process, `testing::test_clipboard()`. Scripts and widgets read and write it instead of the system clipboard, with or without a window. `set_clipboard "text"` and `expect_clipboard "text"` take the rest of the line; quote it to use `\n`. It is emptied by `reset_test_state` and between batch scripts. Call `testing::use_system_clipboard()` after registering to test the platform clipboard.
+
+## E2E isolated storage
+
+Set `AFTERHOURS_TEST_STORAGE_DIR=/some/dir` before `files::init`. Config, saves and temporaries then live in `/some/dir/config/<game>`, `/some/dir/save/<game>` and `/some/dir/tmp/<game>`, and the platform folders are neither read nor created. The settings plugin saves under the save path, so it follows. A host that parses its test directory after `files::init` calls `files::isolate_storage(dir)`, which redirects all three together.
+
+## E2E native resize
+
+`resize w h` changes the layout viewport. `native_resize w h [timeout_s]` resizes the actual window and blocks until `graphics::get_screen_width/height` report `w`x`h` logical points and a UI render has followed. It fails with "unsupported" in headless mode and without a graphics backend. The raylib path is covered by `make -C tests native-window-test`, which opens a hidden window and needs a window server. On sokol/Metal the resize goes through the app's `metal_set_window_size`. Afterhours does not yet provide that function.
+
 ## Image tint
 
 Use `ComponentConfig{}.with_image_tint({255, 120, 60, 200})` with `image`, `sprite`, `image_button`, or `with_texture`. RGB multiplies the source pixels; tint alpha multiplies the widget's opacity and ancestor opacity. Omitting the option restores white tint on a reused widget. Backgrounds and labels keep their own colors.
